From e1b0e8b640d636d3488787cafc47a5aba6c2a4f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:40:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] bwfm: FreeBSD port (sdiob attachment, net80211 glue);
 net80211/ifconfig: firmware WPA PSK

bwfm(4): native Broadcom FullMAC SDIO driver from OpenBSD's.  Chip,
BCDC, firmware-variable and SDIO frame code kept; newbus attachment to
MMCCAM sdiob(4) children (function 1, function 2 found as sibling),
card interrupt polled via CCCR INT_PENDING since sdiob has no interrupt
support, firmware via firmware(9).  net80211: per-device com, cloned
station vap, scan offload fed through ieee80211_add_scan, join from
AUTH, firmware events move the vap to RUN/SCAN, 802.3 data path.

net80211: IEEE80211_IOC_WPAPSK stores a 32-byte PSK in the vap (space
taken from iv_spare, struct size unchanged) for drivers whose firmware
runs the 4-way handshake.

ifconfig: wpakey <passphrase|64 hex> / -wpakey; PBKDF2 done in userland,
WPA, privacy and authmode set along with it.
